# yamllint config for the workflow files in .github/workflows/, the dependabot
# config beside them, and the feed contract in docs/openapi.yaml. The workflows
# are where every merge gate in this repo is defined, so a YAML error in one is
# a gate that stops running rather than a gate that fails, and no other tool in
# the tree parses them: gofmt, staticcheck, vet, biome, ruff, mypy and black all
# read something else. dependabot.yml moves the pins those gates rest on, and
# GitHub reads a broken one the same silent way: no update is offered and the
# tree ages on pins nobody proposed moving. docs/openapi.yaml is the only other
# YAML in the tree, and internal/ingest's test parses it, so a duplicate key or
# a bad indent there is a contract error too.
#
# Extends the default rule set (syntax, indentation, key duplication, trailing
# spaces, colons, brackets), so the finding is a defect and not a taste. The
# three deviations from it, and why:
#
#   line-length 200: the longest line is an actions/checkout pin, `uses:` plus
#     a 40-character SHA plus the release tag. The default 80 would fail every
#     pinned action line, and unwrapping a SHA is not a defect to fix.
#   comments-indentation: the pinned `uses:` lines carry a trailing `# v7.0.1`.
#     That comment names the tag the SHA resolves to, so it stays.
#   truthy: narrowed to values, not disabled. `on:` is a GitHub Actions key and
#     a YAML 1.1 boolean, so the key check trips on line one of every workflow
#     and the key cannot be rewritten without breaking it. The value half is
#     kept, because that is where a real defect lives: a quoted `cache: "false"`
#     or `enable-cache: True` is a string GitHub ignores, so the step runs
#     un-cached or the flag silently does nothing and the run still reports ok.
#     Every boolean value in the workflows is lowercase and unquoted, so
#     check-keys: false is a rule the tree already passes.
#   document-start: a workflow is not a YAML document anyone concatenates or
#     includes, and `---` as its first line is not a GitHub Actions convention.
#     Its absence says nothing about the file being wrong.
extends: default

rules:
  line-length: { max: 200 }
  comments-indentation: disable
  document-start: disable
  truthy: { check-keys: false, level: error }
